    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d411">

                <pb facs="0362" n="350" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg350"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890G.24/38: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-08-11T18:00:00+01:00">August 11, 1942—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 11—3:25 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4483. We took up with the Foreign Office the question set forth in the
                    Department’s telegram No. 3381, July 21, 12 p.m.,<anchor n="16" xml:id="d411-f1"
                    /> and have now received from the Foreign Office an assurance that the British
                    Ambassador at Baghdad has been instructed to consult with our Chargé d’Affaires
                    “and to endeavor to assist him in reaching an agreed solution with the Iraqi
                    Government”.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Baghdad.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
